  "id": "macarthur-scale-of-subjective-social-status",
  "term": "MacArthur Scale of Subjective Social Status",
  "definition": "The MacArthur Scale of Subjective Social Status is a simple self-report measure of socioeconomic status that uses a ladder image to ask people where they see themselves in relation to others in their community. It reflects perceived social standing rather than objective indicators such as income, education, assets, or housing conditions.",
